{"parentUuid":"78b7da84-eef7-45b9-baf9-e019a92d042c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfqroh1bQrg7Rg4Vt7C8M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed `auth.ts` so it no longer touches the token, but the cookie side isn't done. This repo has no server code, and browser JavaScript can't create an `HttpOnly` cookie, so the server has to set it.\n\n**What changed in `auth.ts`:** I removed the `token` export, which read from `localStorage`. In its place is `authFetch`, a thin wrapper around `fetch` that adds `credentials: \"include\"` so the browser sends the auth cookie with each request. Nothing else in the repo imported `token`, so nothing else breaks. Since the old constant is gone, the stale-token and SSR problems from before are gone too.\n\n**What the server needs to do:**\n- **On login,** send the JWT back in a cookie instead of the response body:\n  `Set-Cookie: jwt=<token>; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax; Path=/; Max-Age=<ttl>`\n- **On each request,** read the JWT from that cookie instead of the `Authorization` header.\n- **On logout,** clear it by sending the same cookie with `Max-Age=0`.\n- **Add CSRF protection,** since the browser now attaches the cookie automatically. `SameSite=Lax` covers most cases; for anything that changes state, also add a CSRF token or check the `Origin` header.\n- **If the API is on a different origin,** it must reply with `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true` and name the exact origin in `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`, not `*`.\n\n**Cleanup for existing users:** browsers may still hold the old `jwt` key in `localStorage`. Clearing it once on the client after the new login flow is live (`localStorage.removeItem(\"jwt\")`) removes what an attacker could still steal."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1063,"cache_read_input_tokens":53105,"output_tokens":583,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1063,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":583,"cache_read_input_tokens":53105,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1063,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1063},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"3ae04a7e-c498-48f4-9e30-94696a0b060d","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfqrogkU74AeEUhjs3mSo","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5[1m]","type":"assistant","uuid":"5c1471b2-d3d6-4c88-8dba-1c22039a1048","timestamp":"2026-10-09T02:17:12.430Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","session_id":"81ef4218-b6bb-4f49-aba5-9156edd7320e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/private/tmp/dots-test-repo","sessionId":"81ef4218-b6bb-4f49-aba5-9156edd7320e","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main"}
